---
title: Great horned owl
---
# Great horned owl

The great horned owl is a heavily built nocturnal predator of the Americas,
named for the two feather tufts above a broad facial disc. It has the widest
diet of any American raptor, preying after dark on anything from a beetle to a
skunk or a young raccoon. Territories are announced through the dark hours of
the cold months with a deep series of hoots that carries a kilometre. It
constructs almost nothing of its own, taking over the old stick platform of a
hawk or a squirrel. See [[strigidae]].
